{"parseRefreshTokenResponse's minimumTokenResponseSchema is effectively just {access_token}, causing expiry/refresh_token fields to be stripped under delegation, and it injects a dummy refresh_token value which can overwrite real refresh tokens and produce NaN expiry computations": 0.951046347618103, "GoogleCalendarService stores the Zod safeParse result object into credential.key instead of the credential JSON shape, and delegated refresh returns a fetch Response so res.data is undefined, causing token updates to fail": 0.9865971207618713, "When delegation is enabled, refreshOAuthTokens returns a fetch Response, but multiple integrations expect axios/Gaxios/SDK token objects (with .data / token fields), causing runtime errors and preventing token refresh when CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT is set": 0.9849638342857361, "Zoho Bigin passes credentialId into refreshOAuthTokens where a Cal.com userId is expected, so delegated refresh will call the external endpoint with the wrong identifier, preventing the external app store from locating the correct user tokens": 0.917881965637207, "Salesforce refresh checks response.statusText instead of response.ok, which is unreliable": 0.8026989102363586, "SalesforceCalendarService uses prisma without importing it and instantiates jsforce.Connection using the old access token even after refreshing and storing new tokens": 0.9560170769691467, "The webhook handler does not enforce POST method and performs zod.parse, symmetricDecrypt, and JSON.parse without try/catch, causing invalid payloads or misconfiguration to throw 500s instead of clean 4xx errors": 0.9758978486061096}